    "title": "pandas.Index.fillna — pandas 1.5.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.fillna#\n\n- \nIndex.fillna(*value=None* ,*downcast=None* )[source]#\n- Fill NA/NaN values with the specified value. \n  - Parameters\n    - **value** scalar\n    - Scalar value to use to fill holes (e.g. 0). This value cannot be a list-likes.\n    - **downcast** dict, default is None\n    - A dict of item->dtype of what to downcast if possible, or the string ‘infer’ which will try to downcast to an appropriate equal type (e.g. float64 to int64 if possible).\n  - Returns\n    - Index\n See also \n  - `DataFrame.fillna`\n  - Fill NaN values of a DataFrame.\n  - `Series.fillna`\n  - Fill NaN Values of a Series.",
    "markdown_length": 615,
